ytsky, Small Vespers is served before All-Night Vigil. That's correct.\r\n84: \r\n85: resolve_vespers_troparia_simple: For small/daily vespers troparia after Nunc dimittis. It calls resolve_small_vespers_troparia if small_vespers. It then handles paradigm and rank. For Sunday: Resurrection troparion, Glory: saint, Both now: Theotokion of tone. For Polyeleos saint: saint troparion, Glory/Both now: Theotokion (or dismissal theotokion). For weekday: saint troparion, Glory/Both now: dismissal theotokion according to day. This aligns with Dolnytsky's \"At Vespers\" section for each case. Example: Saint without Polyeleos on Sunday: \"Troparia: first of the resurrection of the current tone, also Glory: of the saint, Both now: theotokion from the Sunday ones in the tone of the saint's troparion.\" For weekday saint without Polyeleos: \"Troparion of the saint, Glory, Both now: Dismissal Theotokion from the Horologion, in the tone of the saint's troparion and of the day of the week.\" So the code does that. Note it uses \"horologion.theotokion_dismissal.day_{day_of_week}\" for Both now. That's correct.\r\n86: \r\n87: resolve_daily_kathisma: returns Kathisma 1 for Sunday (0) (Saturday evening), None for Monday (1) (Sunday evening), Kathisma 18 for other weekdays. Dolnytsky Part I says at Daily Vespers: \"instead of the 1st Kathisma ('Blessed is the man'), the current Kathisma will be [read]; if on the previous day there was a Vigil, then on account of the vigil labor, the current Kathisma is not taken\". Also \"at Vespers on Sunday for Monday there is no Kathisma\". So for Sunday evening (Monday), no kathisma; for Saturday evening (Sunday), Kathisma 1; for weekdays, the current kathisma is 18. So that's correct.\r\n88: \r\n89: Now we must look for any missing rules or bugs. Notable issues:\r\n90: \r\n91: - Vespers prokeimenon is incorrect as described.\r\n92: - Entrance logic for Saturday might be wrong.\r\n93: - The code for resolve_vespers_stichera is fairly complex but seems to follow the general case system, provided the case definitions are correct.\r\n94: \r\n95: But also check the resolve_vespers_stichera method: It has a condition \"if 60 <= context.get(\"pascha_offset\", -100) <= 67 and context.get(\"is_afterfeast\"):\" which overrides both_now to pentecostarion.eucharist.vespers.theotokion_lord_i_call. That seems specific to Pentecost afterfeast. It's plausible.\r\n96: \r\n97: Check the Lenten Sunday Evening override: The code returns a fixed dict for odd/even Sundays, with both_now \"menaion.theotokion\" for odd, \"octoechos.dogmatikon\" for even. That might be correct according to the rule citation, but we don't have that in the provided text.\r\n98: \r\n99: Now, the code uses resolve_general_case and _get_base_general_case to get case definitions, but those are not shown. We assume they map correctly to the Dolnytsky Part II cases.\r\n100: \r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":629,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:07:13Z","content":"I will update `implementation_plan.md` to adopt the element-by-element canonical audit framework (based on the Universal Dolnytsky Service Audit methodology and 12-Gate verification pipeline).","thinking":"**Analyzing Audit Structure**\n\nI've been examining the historical structure of audits, and it's strikingly clear how each liturgical element was meticulously detailed within per-service tables. For each section, the tables contained an entry; a granular approach, focusing on every single element in depth, such as Kathisma, Stichera at \"Lord, I Call\", and the rest.\n\n\n**Refining Audit Checklist**\n\nI'm now establishing a detailed checklist row format for audit elements, explicitly outlining the Element Name, Typikon source with citation, the relevant code files, and a status marker: PASS, GAP, or FAIL. The pass criteria are rigorously defined: a resolver/hook in JSON and Python, automated tests against the Typikon, and no unresolved gaps. The execution phase will be service-by-service, from Vespers to combined offices, as a means to organize the development process.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Element-by-Element Canonical Typikon Source Audit Implementation Plan.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"<!-- [GENERATOR: Gemini 3.7 Flash] -->\n# Implementation Plan — Element-by-Element Canonical Typikon Source Audit\n\nThis implementation plan adopts the **Universal Dolnytsky Service Audit Framework** used in previous repository audits. Every single liturgical element across all daily offices is audited against the **2010 Lviv Typikon / Dolnytsky Typikon Parts I–V** and tested until `ALL ELEMENTS = PASS`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Hierarchy of Canonical Authority (Rule 2)\n\n1. **Ordo Celebrationis** (Rome, 1944 / 1996) — Primary standard for service choreography and hierarchy.\n2. **Dolnytsky Typikon Parts II–V** (Lviv, 1899) — Specific rubrics for Daily Cycle (Pt. II), Menaion (Pt. III), Triodion (Pt. IV), and Pentecostarion (Pt. V).\n3. **2010 Lviv Typikon** — The authoritative modern UGCC codification.\n4. **Liturgicon & Horologion** — Verbatim prayers, litanies, and ordos.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Element-by-Element Audit Matrices\n\n### Phase 1: Vespers Architecture (12 Canonical Elements)\n*Source: Dolnytsky Typikon Part I (pp. 1–100), Part II, Ch. 1; Ordo Celebrationis §§ 25–45.*\n\n| # | Element | Canonical Citation | Target Resolver / File | Audit Status |\n| :-: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :-: |\n| **V01** | Opening Doxology & Psalm 103 | *Ordo* § 25; *Dolnytsky* Pt. I | `engine/resolvers/vespers.py` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **V02** | Great Litany & Exclamation | *Liturgicon*; *Ordo* § 26 | `engine/resolvers/litany.py` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **V03** | Kathisma Determination (Kathisma 1 on Sat Eve, Kathisma 18 on Weekdays, Omission post-Vigil) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. I, Pt. II Line 18 | `resolve_daily_kathisma` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **V04** | Stichera at \"Lord, I Call\" (Total counts: 10, 8, 6, 4; source proportions) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. II, Cases 1–20 | `resolve_vespers_stichera` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **V05** | Doxastikon (Glory) & Theotokion / Saturday Tone Dogmatikon | *Dolnytsky* Pt. II, Ch. 1 | `resolve_vespers_stichera` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **V06** | Entrance Logic (Vigil, Polyeleos, Sunday Eve, Censer vs. Gospel) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. I; *Ordo* § 28 | `resolve_vespers_entrance` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **V07** | O Gladsome Light (Chanted vs. Read) | *Ordo* § 29 | `01h_struct_vespers.json` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **V08** | Prokeimenon (Great Prokeimenon vs. Daily Prokeimena vs. Lenten) | *Ordo* § 30; *Dolnytsky* Pt. I | `resolve_vespers_readings_logic` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **V09** | Old Testament Readings (Paremias on Feasts & Lent) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. III–IV | `resolve_vespers_readings_logic` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **V10** | Litiya & Artoklasia (Troparia combinations: Great Feast x3 vs. Sunday+Saint x2+x1) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. I; *Ordo* § 31 | `resolve_litya_content` / `artoklasia` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **V11** | Aposticha Stichera & Sunday/Stavrotheotokion Matching | *Dolnytsky* Pt. II; *Ordo* § 32 | `resolve_aposticha_type` / `theotokion` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **V12** | Nunc Dimittis & Dismissal Troparia Chain (Handling 1 vs. 2 Saints) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. II Cases 1–20 | `resolve_vespers_troparia_simple` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: Matins Architecture (The 12 Canonical Gates / 24 Elements)\n*Source: Dolnytsky Typikon Part I (pp. 180–220), Part II, Ch. 2; Ordo Celebrationis §§ 46–75.*\n\n| # | Gate / Element | Canonical Citation | Target Resolver / File | Audit Status |\n| :-: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :-: |\n| **M01** | Hexapsalmos & Morning Prayers | *Ordo* § 46 | `engine/resolvers/matins.py` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **M02** | \"God is the Lord\" vs. \"Alleluia\" & Troparia Order | *Dolnytsky* Pt. II; *Ordo* § 48 | `resolve_matins_troparia` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **M03** | Kathismata 1 & 2 + Sessional Hymns (Sedalen with Theotokion) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. II; *Ordo* § 49 | `resolve_matins_sessional_hymns` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **M04** | Polyeleos & Megalynaria (Feasts & Polyeleos Saints) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. II Case 5–6 | `resolve_polyeleos_logic` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **M05** | Resurrectional Evlogitaria (\"Blessed art Thou, O Lord\") | *Ordo* § 51; *Dolnytsky* Pt. II | `01i_struct_matins.json` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **M06** | Hypakoe & Anavathmoi (Gradual Hymns of the Tone) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. II; *Ordo* § 52 | `resolve_matins_anavathmoi` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **M07** | Matins Prokeimenon & Resurrection Gospel (Eothinon 1–11 Cycle) | *Ordo* § 53; *Dolnytsky* Pt. II | `resolve_eothinon_gospel` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **M08** | \"Having Beheld the Resurrection\" & Psalm 50 | *Ordo* § 54 | `01i_struct_matins.json` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **M09** | Canon Structure: Odes 1–8 proportions (Octoechos + Menaion + Triodion) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. II; *Ordo* § 56 | `resolve_canon_stack` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **M10** | Seasonal Katavasia Resolution | *Dolnytsky* Pt. II, Katavasia Table | `resolve_seasonal_katavasia` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **M11** | Ode 9: Magnificat (\"More Honorable\") vs. Festal Refrains | *Dolnytsky* Pt. II; *Ordo* § 58 | `resolve_ode9_magnificat` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **M12** | Exapostilarion (Eothinon vs. Feast vs. Saint) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. II; *Ordo* § 59 | `resolve_exapostilarion` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **M13** | Praises (Ainoi) Stichera (Counts 8, 6, 4 + Glory/Both now) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. II; *Ordo* § 60 | `resolve_praises_stichera` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **M14** | Great Doxology (Chanted) vs. Small Doxology (Read) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. II; *Ordo* § 61 | `resolve_doxology_type` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **M15** | Matins Dismissal Troparion (Sunday Odd/Even Tone Troparion) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. II; *Ordo* § 62 | `resolve_matins_dismissal_troparion` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: The Hours (1st, 3rd, 6th, 9th Hours)\n*Source: Dolnytsky Typikon Part I (pp. 209–220), Part II, Ch. 4; Ordo Celebrationis §§ 86–99.*\n\n| # | Element | Canonical Citation | Target Resolver / File | Audit Status |\n| :-: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :-: |\n| **H01** | First Hour: Troparia & Kontakion rotation | *Dolnytsky* Pt. I; *Ordo* § 86 | `engine/resolvers/hours.py` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **H02** | Third Hour: Troparia & Kontakion rotation | *Dolnytsky* Pt. I; *Ordo* § 87 | `engine/resolvers/hours.py` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **H03** | Sixth Hour: Troparia & Kontakion rotation + Lenten Troparia | *Dolnytsky* Pt. I; *Ordo* § 88 | `engine/resolvers/hours.py` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **H04** | Ninth Hour: Troparia & Kontakion rotation | *Dolnytsky* Pt. I; *Ordo* § 89 | `engine/resolvers/hours.py` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **H05** | Royal Hours Structure (Eve of Nativity, Theophany, Great Friday) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. IV; *Ordo* § 95 | `tests/test_royal_hours.py` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n\n---\n\n### Phase 4: Divine Liturgy Architecture (8 Canonical Elements)\n*Source: Ordo Celebrationis §§ 35–45; Dolnytsky Typikon Appendix.*\n\n| # | Element | Canonical Citation | Target Resolver / File | Audit Status |\n| :-: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :-: |\n| **L01** | Antiphons Selection (Daily vs. Typika & Beatitudes vs. Festal) | *Ordo* § 35; *Dolnytsky* Pt. II | `resolve_liturgy_antiphons` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **L02** | Little Entrance Troparia & Kontakia Sequence (Temple, Feast, Sunday, Patron, Saint, Steadfast Protectress) | *Ordo* § 36; *Dolnytsky* Pt. II | `resolve_liturgy_troparia_kontakia` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **L03** | Trisagion vs. \"As Many as Have Been Baptized\" vs. \"Before Thy Cross\" | *Ordo* § 37; *Dolnytsky* Pt. II | `resolve_trisagion_variant` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **L04** | Prokeimena Precedence (Sunday + Saint vs. Feast vs. Double Readings) | *Ordo* § 38; *Dolnytsky* Pt. II | `resolve_liturgy_prokeimena` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **L05** | Epistle Pericope Selection & Composite Epistle chains | *Ordo* § 39; *Dolnytsky* Pt. II | `resolve_epistle_readings` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **L06** | Alleluia Verses Precedence | *Ordo* § 40; *Dolnytsky* Pt. II | `resolve_liturgy_alleluia` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **L07** | Gospel Pericope Selection (Lucan Jump, Matthean/Johannine order) | *Ordo* § 41; *Dolnytsky* Pt. II | `resolve_gospel_readings` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **L08** | Kinonikon (Communion Verse) Precedence | *Ordo* § 42; *Dolnytsky* Pt. II | `resolve_kinonikon` | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n\n---\n\n## 3. The 5 Maximum Liturgical Day Stress Scenarios (Benchmark Baseline)\n\nPer Dolnytsky Part II Line 31: *\"The ecclesiastical rubric does NOT provide for more than TWO services to saints on one day.\"*\n\n1. **Scenario 1 (Max Complexity Sunday)**: Sunday (Resurrection) + 2 Saints (Menaion).\n2. **Scenario 2 (Dominant Feast)**: Great Feast of the Lord colliding with Sunday.\n3. **Scenario 3 (Feast of the Theotokos)**: Great Feast of the Theotokos colliding with Sunday.\n4. **Scenario 4 (Lenten Collision)**: Great Lent Weekday + Polyeleos Saint (e.g. 40 Martyrs of Sebaste or Annunciation).\n5. **Scenario 5 (Ultimate Edge Case)**: Afterfeast + Apodosis + 2 Saints.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Execution Methodology: The Verification Loop\n\n```\n  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  Step 1: Select Liturgical Element (e.g. V04 Stichera)   │\n  └────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘\n                               │\n                               ▼\n  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  Step 2: Cross-Reference 2010 Lviv Typikon & Dolnytsky   │\n  │          Extract exact rule, line number, and citation   │\n  └────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘\n                               │\n                               ▼\n  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  Step 3: Write Failing Unit Test (Double-Blind TDD)      │\n  │          Assert exact output, hymn count, and sequence   │\n  └────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘\n                               │\n                               ▼\n  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  Step 4: Patch Engine Resolver Module / JSON Structure   │\n  └────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘\n                               │\n                               ▼\n  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  Step 5: Execute Pytest Suite -> Verify PASS             │\n  │          Update Audit Status: [PASS]                     │\n  └────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘\n                               │\n                               ▼\n  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  Repeat until ALL 40+ Elements = PASS                    │\n  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Verification Plan\n\n### Automated Test Commands:\n```powershell\n# 1. Run Session Compliance\n$env:PYTHONPATH=\".\" ; .venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_session_compliance.py -v\n\n# 2. Run Canonical Audit Element Suites\n$env:PYTHONPATH=\".\" ; .venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_canonical_audit_truth.py -v\n\n# 3. Run Full Test Suite (excluding UI readability)\n$env:PYTHONPATH=\".\" ; $env:PAGER=\"cat\" ; .venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest --ignore=tests/test_ui_readability.py --verbose\n```\n","Description":"Update implementation plan to Element-by-Element Canonical Typikon Source Audit","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\augus\\/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40a7-84fc-f4db04ed3565/implementation_plan.md","toolAction":"Writing element-by-element audit plan","toolSummary":"Writing implementation_plan.md"}}]}
