{"step_index":637,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:08:37Z","content":"I will create the implementation plan for the **Cantor Dashboard Panels & UI Elements Audit**, structuring it element-by-element across every interactive control, metadata badge, document viewer, and layout split.","thinking":"**Auditing the Panel**\n\nI've shifted focus. The user corrected me, so I'm now concentrating on auditing the panel. I've set aside the information about matins and vespers, as it's not relevant. The cantor dashboard is the primary concern, so I'm diving back into that, and I'm putting the panel front and center.\n\n\n**Examining the UI**\n\nI'm now fully focused on the Cantor Dashboard UI. The user's input clarified the need for an element-by-element audit of the panels and controls. I've begun to examine the dashboard, specifically the top bar, liturgical date resolver, and control bar. I'm noting the logo, navigation tabs (Liturgical Calendar, Book Browser, Feast & Roadmap), theme toggle, and Recension badge, as well as the date picker and resolve control.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Elements**\n\nI'm now deep in the details of the Liturgical Parameter Overrides drawer, breaking down each control. I'm noting the recension source, Paschalion calendar system, and calendar source options, as well as the Temple Patronal Feast input and ceremonial rubrics. I'm also considering the Digest Layout Mode, developer tools toggle, and active parish profile management. Moving next to Panel 1.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Cantor Dashboard Panels and UI Elements Comprehensive Audit Plan.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"<!-- [GENERATOR: Gemini 3.7 Flash] -->\n# Implementation Plan — Cantor Dashboard Panels & UI Elements Audit\n\nThis plan establishes an element-by-element verification audit of all panels, controls, and data bindings in the **Cantor Dashboard** ([index.html](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/index.html), [main.js](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/main.js), and [style.css](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/style.css)) until `ALL ELEMENTS = PASS`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Dashboard Architecture & Panel Layout\n\nThe Cantor Dashboard is composed of 5 primary panel groups:\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                 CANTOR DASHBOARD HEADER                                │\n│ [Tab: Liturgical Calendar]  [Tab: Book Browser]  [Tab: Feast & Roadmap]  [Theme Toggle]│\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ LITURGICAL DATE RESOLVER BAR                                                           │\n│ [Date Input] [Resolve Date] [Quick Jumps: Clean Monday | Thomas Sunday | Today | etc.] │\n│ [▼ Liturgical Parameter Overrides Drawer]                                              │\n├────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┤\n│ PANEL 1:               │ PANEL 2:                      │ PANEL 3:                      │\n│ LITURGICAL CONTEXT     │ CANTOR SERVICE BOOKLET        │ SERVICE RUBRICS DIGEST        │\n│                        │ (Main View)                   │ (Unified Reference Drawer)    │\n│ • Date & Human Title   │ • Propers & Sung Chants       │ • View Office Dropdown        │\n│ • Rank & Tone Badges   │ • Actor Tags ([PRIEST], etc.) │ • Copy Rubrics Button         │\n│ • Vestment Color Swatch│ • Musical Phrasing Markings   │ • Step-by-Step Rubrics        │\n│ • Fasting Rule Badge   │ • Copy & Print Actions        │ • Vestment & Fasting Badges   │\n│ • Prostrations Rule    │ • [📖 Toggle Reference Panel] │ • Close [❌] Action           │\n│ • Paradigm ID & Types  │                               │                               │\n├────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┤\n│ PANEL 4: ENGINE LOGIC TRACE (Dev Mode Drawer)                                          │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Element-by-Element Dashboard Audit Matrix\n\n### Section A: Resolver Controls & Parameter Overrides\n| # | Element ID | UI Control Description | Data Binding & Expected Behavior | Status |\n| :-: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :-: |\n| **A01** | `liturgical-date-input` | Date Picker | Sets `state.selectedDate`, formats to `YYYY-MM-DD`. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **A02** | `resolve-date-btn` | Primary Action Button | Triggers `/api/resolve` fetch with active query params. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **A03** | `quick-btn` (x4) | Preset Date Shortcuts | Instantly populates date for Clean Monday, Thomas Sun, Today, Dormition. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **A04** | `opt-recension` | Recension Dropdown | Switches text source (Stamford, Royal Doors, St. Sergius). | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **A05** | `opt-calendar-source` | Calendar Source Dropdown | Decoupled calendar rule selector (Default, UGCC Web, Lviv Typikon). | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **A06** | `opt-paschalion` | Paschalion Dropdown | Toggles Gregorian vs. Julian vs. Revised Julian Easter computus. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **A07** | `opt-temple-feast` | Temple Feast Override | Accepts `MM-DD` patronal override and applies feast elevation. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **A08** | `opt-include-ceremonial` | Sanctuary Rubrics Checkbox | Toggles priest/deacon sanctuary choreography inside booklet. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **A09** | `opt-digest-mode` | Full vs. Quick Radio | Toggles comprehensive vs. abbreviated digest layout. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **A10** | `chk-dev-mode` | Dev Tools Checkbox | Shows/hides Panel 4 (`trace-card` / debug logs). | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **A11** | `opt-profile` / `btn-save-profile` | Parish Profile Manager | Persists/loads custom parish parameter bundles from localStorage. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n\n---\n\n### Section B: Panel 1 — Liturgical Context Sidebar\n| # | Element ID | Display Component | Verification Criteria | Status |\n| :-: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :-: |\n| **B01** | `context-spinner` | Loading Indicator | Visible during fetch, hidden on response/error. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **B02** | `context-title` | Human Feast/Day Title | Formats clear feast header with date. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **B03** | `badge-rank` | Dolnytsky Feast Rank Badge | Displays correct Rank (1 to 7) with color-coded badge. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **B04** | `badge-tone` | Tone of the Week Badge | Displays Tone 1–8 with Octoechos mode info. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **B05** | `badge-color` | Vestment Color Swatch | Renders canonical color swatch (Gold, White, Red, Blue, Purple, Green). | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **B06** | `badge-fasting` | Fasting Rule Badge | Renders strict, wine/oil, fish, or fast-free rule with tooltip. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **B07** | `badge-prostrations` | Prostrations Rule | Displays \"Allowed\" vs. \"Forbidden\" with canonical reason. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **B08** | `paradigm-id` | Canonical Paradigm Box | Displays active CASE number (e.g. `CASE_01_SUNDAY_SIMPLE`). | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **B09** | `service-types-list` | Service Combination Grid | Displays resolved service types (Vespers, Matins, Liturgy, Hours). | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n\n---\n\n### Section C: Panel 2 — Cantor Service Booklet\n| # | Element ID | Component | Verification Criteria | Status |\n| :-: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :-: |\n| **C01** | `booklet-content` | Chants & Propers Stream | Formats liturgical texts with drop caps, red rubrics, and bold verses. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **C02** | `actor` tags | Actor Badges | Renders `[PRIEST]:`, `[DEACON]:`, `[CANTOR]:` with styled badges. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **C03** | `cross-icon` | Liturgical Crosses | Renders blessing crosses (`✚`) cleanly in gold/accent styling. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **C04** | `btn-copy-booklet` | Copy Booklet Text Button | Copies plaintext booklet to clipboard with success toast notification. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **C05** | `print-booklet-btn` | Print View Button | Opens print stylesheet formatted for 8.5x11 booklet printing. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **C06** | `btn-toggle-reference` | Toggle Reference Button | Opens/closes Panel 3 and smoothly animates the split view width. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n\n---\n\n### Section D: Panel 3 — Service Rubrics Digest (Unified Reference Panel)\n| # | Element ID | Component | Verification Criteria | Status |\n| :-: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :-: |\n| **D01** | `service-digest-select` | Office Filter Dropdown | Switches between `All Services`, `General Info`, `Vespers`, `Matins`, `Liturgy`, `Hours`. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **D02** | `service-digest-content` | Rubrics Card Renderer | Formats step-by-step liturgical rubrics inside glass cards with titles. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **D03** | `metadata-badge` | Section Vestment/Fasting | Renders office-specific vestment/fasting badges extracted from digest. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **D04** | `btn-copy-digest` | Copy Rubrics Button | Copies full markdown digest when \"All\" is active, or isolated office text when filtered. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **D05** | `btn-close-reference` | Close Drawer Button (`❌`) | Closes the panel and restores Panel 2 to 100% full width. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **D06** | `reference-resize` | Split Resize Drag Handle | Allows dragging to customize width ratio between Booklet and Digest. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n\n---\n\n### Section E: Navigation & Secondary Tabs\n| # | Element ID | Component | Verification Criteria | Status |\n| :-: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :-: |\n| **E01** | `theme-toggle-btn` | Light / Dark Mode Toggle | Toggles `dark-theme` class on `<body>` and persists to localStorage. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **E02** | `tab-browser` | Liturgical Book Browser | Searches all database keys, displays standardized text diffs. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n| **E03** | `tab-roadmap` | Feast & Roadmap Tab | Generates interactive annual calendar feast timeline for active year. | `[PENDING AUDIT]` |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Execution & Verification Workflow\n\n```\n  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  Step 1: Inspect Element (Markup + JS Event + CSS State)  │\n  └─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘\n                                │\n                                ▼\n  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  Step 2: Execute Live UI / API Verification Test          │\n  └─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘\n                                │\n                                ▼\n  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  Step 3: Fix Broken Bindings / Styling Gaps               │\n  └─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘\n                                │\n                                ▼\n  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  Step 4: Mark Element [PASS] and Proceed to Next          │\n  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Verification Plan\n\n### Automated Test Commands:\n```powershell\n# 1. Run Server Endpoint Integration Suite\n$env:PYTHONPATH=\".\" ; .venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_server_endpoints.py -v\n\n# 2. Run Session Compliance Check\n$env:PYTHONPATH=\".\" ; .venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_session_compliance.py -v\n\n# 3. Run Full Test Suite (excluding UI readability)\n$env:PYTHONPATH=\".\" ; $env:PAGER=\"cat\" ; .venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest --ignore=tests/test_ui_readability.py --verbose\n```\n","Description":"Create Cantor Dashboard Panels & UI Elements Audit Implementation Plan","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\augus\\/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40a7-84fc-f4db04ed3565/implementation_plan.md","toolAction":"Writing Cantor Dashboard audit plan","toolSummary":"Writing implementation_plan.md"}}]}
