{"step_index":649,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:10:19Z","content":"I will view the General Info generation logic in `engine/generation.py` using `view_file` to analyze the exact code that constructs Card 1.","thinking":"**Analyzing Visual Inputs**\n\nI've begun analyzing the recently uploaded images. The first image seems to be a \"GENERAL INFO\" card from the Service Rubrics Digest, showing vestment details (\"BRIGHT (RED)\") and a Typicon reference (\"MONDAY, AUGUST 24TH, 202\"). I'm processing the implications of these details now.\n\n\n**Detailing Liturgical Structure**\n\nI'm now integrating the additional image data, focusing on the liturgical structure for the saint's day. I've documented the \"DAILY VESPERS,\" \"SMALL COMPLINE,\" \"MIDNIGHT OFFICE,\" and \"DAILY MATINS\" routines. Currently, I'm noting specific details like the absence of a kathisma at Vespers, the use of Theotokion canons, and the troparia for different services, with reference to the Octoechos. I'm building a cohesive picture now.\n\n\n**Structuring Liturgical Analysis**\n\nI'm now focusing on structuring the liturgical analysis as per the user's guidance. I'm prioritizing the Service Rubrics Digest panel. The directive is crystal clear: Audit each card sequentially, from \"General Info\" through \"Divine Liturgy,\" only progressing once each one \"passes.\" This compartmentalized approach feels incredibly efficient for comprehensive coverage.\n\n\n**Auditing Service Rubrics**\n\nI'm now diving into the specifics. I'm starting with the \"General Info\" card, cross-referencing generated rubrics against the 2010 Lviv Typikon and the Dolnytsky text. I've noted discrepancies in vestment details (the red vestment for St. Eutyches requires validation) and Tone assignments. I'm focusing on the Monday Prokeimenon (is it really IV?), and Matins Dismissal Theotokion (should it be Tone I?). The aim is \"PASS\" for Card 1 before moving on.\n\n\n**Validating Menaion Detail**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the \"Daily Vespers\" card details. It's crucial to confirm the specifics for St. Eutyches, a Hieromartyr. I'm focusing on the number of stichera at \"At Lord, I Call...\" for a simple saint on a weekday. I need to verify whether the service's digest incorrectly states \"6 Stichera to the Saint,\" or the actual combination of Octoechos and Menaion stichera, as described by Dolnytsky's Typikon. I need to get this point correct, and then validate the rest of the generated rubrics for this card.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"c:\\Users\\augus\\OneDrive\\Documents\\Google Antigravity\\Projects\\Typikon Coded\\engine\\generation.py","EndLine":80,"StartLine":1,"toolAction":"Viewing General Info generation in engine/generation.py","toolSummary":"Viewing General Info digest builder"}}]}
{"step_index":650,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:10:28Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-24T19:10:28-04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-08-24T19:10:28-04:00\nFile Path: `file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/engine/generation.py`\nTotal Lines: 1966\nTotal Bytes: 102637\nShowing lines 1 to 80\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: \"\"\"\r\n2: Ruthenian Engine - GenerationMixin\r\n3: Extracted from ruthenian_engine.py during Phase 1 modularization.\r\n4: \"\"\"\r\n5: \r\n6: import json\r\n7: import os\r\n8: import re\r\n9: from datetime import date, timedelta\r\n10: import copy\r\n11: \r\n12: from typikon_digest_generator import TypikonDigestGenerator\r\n13: from engine.utils.type_utils import parse_rank_integer\r\n14: \r\n15: \r\n16: class GenerationMixin:\r\n17: \r\n18:     \"\"\"Mixin providing generation methods for RuthenianEngine.\"\"\"\r\n19: \r\n20: \r\n21:     def resolve_service_combination_header(self, context, rubrics=None):\r\n22:         \"\"\"\r\n23:         NEW-4: Generates the Dolnytsky-style header describing how services combine.\r\n24:         \r\n25:         E.g.: \"Sunday service combined with the Triodion, and that of the forefeast\"\r\n26:         Citation: Dolnytsky Part 2 — Headers of all 20 Paradigms\r\n27:         \"\"\"\r\n28:         components = []\r\n29:         day_of_week = context.get(\"day_of_week\", 0)\r\n30:         season = context.get(\"season_id\", \"\")\r\n31:         d_title = context.get(\"dolnytsky_title\", \"\")\r\n32:         full_text = f\"{d_title}\".lower()\r\n33:         \r\n34:         # Base service\r\n35:         if day_of_week == 0:\r\n36:             components.append(\"Sunday service from the Octoechos\")\r\n37:         e