{"step_index":676,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:15:13Z","content":"I will write the complete reference document `.agents/references/canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md` to permanently codify the canonical maximalist audit standard for all 7 digest cards.","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Authoritative reference codifying the Canonical Maximalist Typikon Digest Standard across all 7 cards.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Canonical Maximalist Typikon Digest Standard\n\n> **Authority**: 2010 Lviv Typikon; Dolnytsky Typikon Parts I–V (1899); Ordo Celebrationis (1944/1996).  \n> **Status**: Immutable Authoritative Standard for Service Rubrics Digest Cards.\n\n---\n\n## Overview & Purpose\nThis standard defines the **Canonical Maximalist Specification** for every card in the **Service Rubrics Digest**. A card is considered canonically complete and marked `PASS` if and only if it satisfies all required checkpoints below with zero omitted, summarized, or hallucinated rubrics.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Hierarchy of Canonical Authority (Rule 